From efe2ccab1744b9df2c549cad11ebd8312b4a93ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:14:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fuse TP1 embedding ID normalization into lookup

Upstream base: 44d3a36923fcaf78b36aee4a789000276b571b2c. Rationale: actual request call origins show clamp_min and int64 casts immediately before TP1 embedding. TileLang methods consume native int32/int64 strides and clamp negative multimodal IDs inside the lookup; plain tables use TileLang too. Quality: opaque BF16 payloads and negative-ID-to-row-zero semantics are preserved; tensor-parallel lookup keeps its original non-clamping specialization. Other quantization methods retain their existing preprocessing. Tests: 36 new public eager/graph cases cover plain/packed tables, ID widths, empty and shifted/strided/matrix IDs; existing parallel cases and declaration checks; GPU/performance validation pending. Lint: one inherited long CUDA-header line. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
